&#8220;THE POP PARTY RETURNS TO THE MONUMENTAL!&#8221; she shared in an Instagram post Monday (Aug. 3). “I&#8217;m writing this and I can&#8217;t believe it. But you guys just won&#8217;t stop calling on the devil!! You know where I&#8217;ll be on September 26th!”

In a video promotion, the Argentine artist makes her way to the stadium while narrating in Spanish: &#8220;I was never what they wanted me to be, and I don&#8217;t care — there are always those who were truly there for me; the rest don&#8217;t matter. And whatever people might say, it doesn&#8217;t bother me anymore. They know where to find me whenever they want.&#8221;

In the background, her punk tune &#8220;No Me Importa&#8221; from the 2025 album No Vayas a Atender Cuando el Demonio Llama plays.

Lali’s forthcoming concert marks her third show at the venue formerly known as Estadio River Plate; it has a capacity of more than 85,000 people. She previously had two sold-out shows on June 6 and 7, where she featured special guests such as Dillom, Miranda!, Duki and Kylie Minogue.

Additionally, the Sept. 26 show — which wraps her No Vayas a Atender Cuando el Demonio Llama tour — will coincide with the two-year anniversary of the release of her song “Fanático,” which introduced her new era as an edgy pop rock star. “Fanático” peaked at No. 5 on the Billboard Argentina Hot 100 in October 2024, becoming Lali’s biggest hit to date.

Ticket presales will begin at 11 a.m. local time in Argentina on Wednesday, Aug. 5, via AllAccess .

